    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The fruit bowl and its projection.</b> We can read the symbols on the bowl (X, heart, banana) and we can see the blue projection land on it, but we could not tie either to a lock with confidence, and we did not find a panel in this room that accepts shapes. No shape-to-digit mapping is printed here because any mapping we gave you would be invented.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The playing cards.</b> Three cards go into the bag and none of them is used in any shot we captured. Whether they feed a lock in this room, a lock later in Chapter 3, or nothing at all, we do not know.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The nutcracker and the lighter.</b> Both appear in the inventory; neither action is shown clearly. The nutcracker is probably what reveals the second paper, and the lighter is never used in the footage at all. Both are listed as collected items, not as steps.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The reward and the exit.</b> The recording ends at 2:42 on a THANKS FOR WATCHING card, before any results panel. We do not print a coin reward for this room because we have not seen one. If you finish the level yourself, the results card is the thing to check.
